<description>
Complete the sparse-color reflected copy of the foreground motif across its matching marker row or column.

Input structure
- The grid has one background color and two foreground colors.
- One foreground color appears only as a sparse marker row or column.
- The other foreground color contains the same sparse marker positions on a parallel row or column, plus the motif on the far side of the sparse markers.

Rule
- Keep the original grid unchanged.
- Reflect every motif pixel of the larger foreground color across the two parallel marker lines.
- Paint the reflected motif pixels with the sparse marker color.

Key insight
- The two equal marker rows or columns are paired landmarks: the sparse-color marker line borders the source motif, and the matching source-color marker line anchors the reflected copy.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "larger foreground color: motif on one side of a sparse marker row or column, plus a matching marker line",
  "dst": "background cells beyond the matching source-color marker line",
  "transform": "reflect the motif across the pair of parallel marker lines and recolor it to the sparse marker color; keep all original pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22x22 [observed]
  colors: 1 background + 2 foreground (marker_color, source_color)
  axis: row or col (determines orientation of all structures)
  marker_line:
    description: single row/col of marker_color at evenly-spaced positions
    count: 6-8 positions
    spacing: 3-4 (uniform)
    range: first position at 0, last at or near grid edge [observed]
  source_marker_line:
    description: parallel row/col of source_color at identical positions
    gap: 4-6 cells from marker_line, on opposite side from body
  body:
    description: 4-connected motif in source_color on the far side of marker_line from source_line
    depth: 3-6 cells from marker_line (must be <= gap)
    cross_span: covers first-to-last marker position (may extend 1 cell past)
    adjacent: body row/col next to marker_line has a pixel at each marker position [observed]
    pixel_count: 30-45
  layout_along_axis: body | marker_line | bg gap | source_line | (empty for reflection)
  transform: reflect body across midpoint of (marker_line, source_line), paint with marker_color
  output_grid: same size, input preserved, reflected body added in marker_color on bg cells

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid 22x22, 3 distinct colors (bg, marker_color, source_color), axis (row or col)
    2. Choose marker spacing (3-4) and count (6-8); place marker positions starting at 0
    3. Choose body depth D (3-6) and gap G (D to D+2); place marker_line so body fits on one side
    4. Set source_line = marker_line + G (or - G) on the other side; ensure reflection fits in grid
    5. Draw both marker lines (marker_color and source_color at the same positions)
    6. Generate a random 4-connected body on the body side of marker_line, depth <= D, spanning all marker positions; ensure it touches the marker-adjacent row/col at each marker position
